WEBVTT
NOTE Synthetic interview written for intavue's eval set (not real participant data).

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:06.000
<v Interviewer>Thanks for joining. To start, how do you usually get your groceries?

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:19.000
<v Participant>Mostly delivery now. Since the baby I do almost everything through the app on Sunday night, after she's asleep. I start from last week's order and edit it.

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:22.000
<v Interviewer>Why Sunday night specifically?

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:38.000
<v Participant>It's the only quiet time. And the Monday morning slots fill up, so if I wait until Monday it's Wednesday before anything arrives. I learned that the hard way when we ran out of formula.

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:41.000
<v Interviewer>Do you use any other apps?

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:55.000
<v Participant>Sometimes the corner shop's WhatsApp for bread and eggs, the owner just sends a voice note back. And my partner has his own app for the big Costco run, which honestly causes a lot of double buying.

00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:59.000
<v Interviewer>What happens when something is out of stock?

00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:16.000
<v Participant>Substitutions are a lottery. Last month they replaced oat milk with condensed milk. Now I tick "no substitutions" for anything the baby eats, but then I just get gaps and have to go to the shop anyway.

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:20.000
<v Interviewer>Is price important to you when you shop online?

00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:30.000
<v Participant>Yes. I compare the basket total with the supermarket flyer sometimes. Delivery fees add up, so I try to hit the free-delivery minimum.

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:33.000
<v Interviewer>Great, that's really helpful, thank you.
